session:pr650Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #510 (split from the #373 owl2rdf umbrella) asked for the RDF encoding of SubObjectPropertyOf(ObjectPropertyChain(...) OPE) -- owl2rl2datalog::owl_to_rdf's object_property_axiom only handled the single-property SubObjectPropertyExpression case and silently fell through the catch-all skip for the PropertyExpressionChain variant. Checked provenance for owl_to_rdf.rs/owl2rl2datalog first (PRs #370/#374/#433): confirmed the module's established pattern of resolving each property/class expression via a fallible named_* helper and recording an unresolvable member in RdfTranslationReport::skipped rather than partially emitting triples, and that Translator::rdf_list (added for DisjointUnionOf) was reusable as-is since the issue's own text anticipated that. Before writing code, read rdf_owl_translator/src/axiom_parser.rs's existing owl:propertyChainAxiom read-back arm to pin down the exact triple shape rather than trusting memory of the W3C spec table: the predicate hangs off the *super*-property (triple.subject in the parser), with the rdf:List of chain members as the object -- matches Table 18 of the OWL 2 Mapping to RDF Graphs spec. Followed strict TDD: wrote four tests first (#[ignore]d) covering a 2-member chain, a 3-member chain (list order), axiom-annotation reification via owl:Axiom (mirroring the module's existing triple_p_annotated convention), and a skip case for a chain containing an unsupported member (an inverse property expression, since named_object_property only resolves named/anonymous properties). Implemented a single new match arm in object_property_axiom mirroring the existing SubObjectPropertyExpression arm's shape: resolve every chain member via named_object_properties, resolve the super-property via named_object_property, build the rdf:List via the existing helper, then emit one triple_p_annotated call. All four tests passed unmodified once the arm was added -- no iteration needed since the existing helpers already had exactly the right shape. Local `cargo test --workspace` hit one unrelated SIGKILL in sparql-endpoint's query_timeout test, traced to heavy concurrent cargo activity from several other agent worktrees running in parallel on the same machine (confirmed via `ps aux`), not this change; real CI (isolated) came back fully green across all 8 jobs." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:650 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr650 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
